-- title:
--   Genus of quotients of the Drinfeld curve by μ_{q+1}
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field equipped with an algebra structure over the field $\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2$ with $q^2$ elements, and assume that the coordinate ring `CoordRing q k`, namely the quotient of the polynomial ring $k[X_0,X_1]$ in two variables by the principal ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`, is a domain; write $F$ for its fraction field `drinfeldFunctionField q k`. Let $C$ be a subgroup of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2$, and let $d$ be a natural number with $d\cdot\#C = q+1$. Each $\zeta \in C$ gives an element of `hSubgroup q`, the kernel of `hChar q` inside $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)\times \mathbb{F}_{q^2}^\times$ (membership witnessed by `one_mem_hSubgroup_of_mem q ζ`), and hence, through `hFunctionFieldAction q k`, a $k$-algebra automorphism of $F$; let $G$ be the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_k(F)$ generated by these automorphisms and let $F^{G}$ be the corresponding fixed intermediate field. The assertion is the equality of natural numbers $$2\cdot \mathrm{genusFF}\,k\,F^{G} = (d-1)(q-1),$$ where $\mathrm{genusFF}\,k\,F^{G}$ is the $k$-dimension of $H^1$ of the zero divisor of $F^{G}/k$, and the subtractions are truncated subtraction of natural numbers.
--
--   This is the genus computation for the quotients of the Drinfeld (Deligne–Lusztig) curve $xy^q-x^qy=1$ by the subgroups $C$ of the group $\mu_{q+1}$ of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity, stated in the division-free form $2g=(d-1)(q-1)$ with $d$ the index of $C$. It is used by [`DrinfeldCurve.natCard_mul_two_mul_genusFF_quotField_add_eq`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.natCard_mul_two_mul_genusFF_quotField_add_eq).
